  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "snFtxhpqxohsomEkDgMzY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -113.96440972222229,
      "y": -536.3541666666666,
      "width": 658.5611979166667,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 204456109,
      "version": 860,
      "versionNonce": 771807715,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793131638802,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements:\n- Indentify user -> By userId, IP or API Key\n    - An API key identifies the application, a UserID identifies the\nperson, and an IP address identifies the network connection\n- Limit Requests based of a configurable rule\n- Return proper statuc code and error headers\n\nScale:\n- 100M DAU\n- 1M rps\n\nNon-Functional Requirements:\n- Availability >> Consistency\n- Low Latency rate limit checks (<10ms)\n- Scalable to 1M rps\n\n\n\nCore Entities:\n- Request\n- Client (userId, Ip or API Key)\n- Rule (100 req/min/user)\n\n\n\nSystem Interface:\nisRequestAllowed(userId, ruleId) -> \n{\n    passes: boolean,\n    statusCode: STATUS_CODE,\n    message: string,\n    remaining: number,\n    resetTime: timestamp\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements:\n- Indentify user -> By userId, IP or API Key\n    - An API key identifies the application, a UserID identifies the person, and an IP address identifies the network connection\n- Limit Requests based of a configurable rule\n- Return proper statuc code and error headers\n\nScale:\n- 100M DAU\n- 1M rps\n\nNon-Functional Requirements:\n- Availability >> Consistency\n- Low Latency rate limit checks (<10ms)\n- Scalable to 1M rps\n\n\n\nCore Entities:\n- Request\n- Client (userId, Ip or API Key)\n- Rule (100 req/min/user)\n\n\n\nSystem Interface:\nisRequestAllowed(userId, ruleId) -> \n{\n    passes: boolean,\n    statusCode: STATUS_CODE,\n    message: string,\n    remaining: number,\n    resetTime: timestamp\n}",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BE8wcLF0Drh4vVKekzrtE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 606.5106336805557,
      "y": -539.9170386904766,
      "width": 957.8125000000001,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 293856579,
      "version": 1330,
      "versionNonce": 1058941229,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793131632563,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Where should we put the rate-limiter\n2. How should we identify clients\n\n- Both questions are dependent on each other or can answer other question\n- The placement of the rate-limiter can tell us how muhc of client information is accessible\n\nWe can put Rate-Limiter at below mentioned places\n1. In each micro-services -> part of its code\n    - Super fast, In-memory check. Downside: No global count management. 2 requests of client\nmade to different service -> For those services, client made only 1 request\n2. A seperate service/instance\n    - Gloabl counter. Each MS calls this service. Excess latency. Request comes to gateway ->\ngoes to MS -> MS checks Ratelimiter service\n3. Add Rate-Limiter in the gateway\n    - Issues: Scale side issue. It limits the amount of context that we have\n    - Put rate-limiter configs for each users in a Redis cache to make it shared for all instances\nof Gateway services",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Where should we put the rate-limiter\n2. How should we identify clients\n\n- Both questions are dependent on each other or can answer other question\n- The placement of the rate-limiter can tell us how muhc of client information is accessible\n\nWe can put Rate-Limiter at below mentioned places\n1. In each micro-services -> part of its code\n    - Super fast, In-memory check. Downside: No global count management. 2 requests of client made to different service -> For those services, client made only 1 request\n2. A seperate service/instance\n    - Gloabl counter. Each MS calls this service. Excess latency. Request comes to gateway -> goes to MS -> MS checks Ratelimiter service\n3. Add Rate-Limiter in the gateway\n    - Issues: Scale side issue. It limits the amount of context that we have\n    - Put rate-limiter configs for each users in a Redis cache to make it shared for all instances of Gateway services",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
